/-!
# The function field and the local rings of an irreducible projective plane curve

Let `F ∈ k[X₀, X₁, X₂]` be an irreducible form, so that the homogeneous ideal `(F)` (Tau Ceti's
`projectivePlaneCurve.ideal`) is prime. The function field `k(C)` of the curve `C = V(F)` and its
local ring `𝒪_P(C)` at a point `P ∈ C` are the function field and the local rings of this
homogeneous prime (`ProjectiveSpace.functionField`, `ProjectiveSpace.localSubring`).

Restricting functions from the plane to `C`, `G / H ↦ Ḡ / H̄`, is a surjective map
`𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` with kernel `(F_*)`, so that `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*)`
(Fulton, §5.1). This is first proved for any homogeneous prime `I` of `k[X₀, …, Xₙ]` and
`P ∈ V(I)`: the restriction `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) → 𝒪_P(V(I))` is surjective with kernel the localized ideal
`I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)`.

In a chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0` containing `P`, dehomogenization `f / g ↦ f_(i) / g_(i)` identifies `k(C)` with
the function field `k(F_(i))` of the affine curve `F_(i) = 0` and `𝒪_P(C)` with its local ring
`𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))`, and so, by Problem 2.44, with `𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))` (Fulton, §4.3 and
§5.1). For every form `F`, irreducible or not, the chart isomorphism
`𝒪_P(ℙ²) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²)` gives `𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))`.

The function field `k(C)` is the function field of Tau Ceti's integral scheme
`projectivePlaneCurve hF`, the `Proj` of `k[X₀, X₁, X₂] ⧸ (F)`: in every chart `Xᵢ` with `F ∤ Xᵢ`,
the fraction `p / Xᵢᵐ` is the germ of the function `p / Xᵢᵐ` on `D₊(Xᵢ)`. It is an algebraic
function field of one variable over `k`.

## Main definitions

* `PlaneCurves.Projective.toVarietyLocalRing I P : 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) →ₐ[k] 𝒪_P(V)`: the restriction of
  functions, `f / g ↦ f̄ / ḡ`, for a homogeneous ideal `I` and `P ∈ V(I)`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.quotientLocalIdealEquiv I P`: `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ⧸ I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ≅ 𝒪_P(V)`, for a
  homogeneous prime `I`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.functionField hF`: the function field `k(C)` of the curve `F = 0`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.localSubring hF P`: the local ring `𝒪_P(C)`, a local subring of `k(C)`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.toLocalSubring hF P : 𝒪_P(ℙ²) →ₐ[k] 𝒪_P(C)`: the restriction of
  functions to `C`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P`: `𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_P(C)`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.quotientSpanPairEquiv hF P G`: `𝒪_P(C) ⧸ (Ḡ_*) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*, G_*)`,
  where `Ḡ_*` is the restriction of `G_*` to `C`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv hF hP`:
  `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸ⁿ) ⧸ (F_(i))`, for every form `F`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi`: `k(C) ≅ k(F_(i))`, for `F ∤ Xᵢ`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP`: `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv hF i P hP`:
  `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))`.
* `PlaneCurves.Projective.functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv hF`: `k(C)` is the function
  field of Tau Ceti's `projectivePlaneCurve hF`.

## Main results

* `ker_toVarietyLocalRing`: the kernel of the restriction `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) → 𝒪_P(V)` is `I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)`.
* `mem_localSubring_iff`: `z ∈ 𝒪_P(C)` iff `z = f / g` for forms of the same degree with
  `g(P) ≠ 0`.
* `ker_toLocalSubring`: the kernel of `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` is `(F_*)`.
* `map_toLocalSubring_span_pair`: for every `G`, the image of `(F_*, G_*)` in `𝒪_P(C)` is the
  ideal `(Ḡ_*)` generated by the restriction of `G_*`.
* `isPrime_toIdeal_ideal`: for an irreducible form `F`, the ideal `(F)` is prime.
* `not_X_dvd_of_mem_affineOpen`: for `P ∈ C` with `Xᵢ(P) ≠ 0`, `Xᵢ ∤ F`, so that `F_(i)` is
  irreducible of degree `d`.
* `functionField.chartEquiv_mk`, `localSubring.coe_chartEquiv`: the chart isomorphisms send
  `f / g` to `f_(i) / g_(i)`, the second is the restriction of the first.
* `localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_toLocalSubring`,
  `localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_quotientLocalEquationEquiv`: compatibility of
  `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))` with the restriction and the chart of `ℙ²`.
* `localSubring_spec`: the milestone, parts (a) and (b) and the form for every `F`.
* `functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_mk`,
  `functionField.functionFieldEquiv_schemeFunctionFieldEquiv`: the isomorphism with Tau Ceti's
  function field sends `p / Xᵢᵐ` to the germ of `p / Xᵢᵐ` on `D₊(Xᵢ)`, in every chart with
  `F ∤ Xᵢ`, and agrees with `projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv` in every such chart.
* `functionField.isFunctionField`: `k(C)` is an algebraic function field of one variable.

## References

* [W. Fulton, *Algebraic Curves*][Fulton2008], §4.3, §5.1
-/

public section

open MvPolynomial Projectivization PlaneCurves.ProjectiveSpace HomogeneousLocalization
open TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped LinearAlgebra.Projectivization

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

namespace TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectivePlaneCurve

variable {k : Type*} [Field k] {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} {d : ℕ}

/-- The homogeneous ideal `(F)` of an irreducible form `F` is prime. The variables are written
`Fin (2 + 1)`, so that the instance is found both for `Fin 3` and where the plane is `ℙⁿ` with
`n = 2`, as for `ProjectiveSpace.functionField`. -/
instance isPrime_toIdeal_ideal (hF : F.IsHomogeneous d) [Fact (Irreducible F)] :
    @Ideal.IsPrime (MvPolynomial (Fin (2 + 1)) k) _
      (HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal (𝒜 := homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (2 + 1)) k) (ideal hF)) := by
  rw [toIdeal_ideal, Ideal.span_singleton_prime (Fact.out : Irreducible F).ne_zero]
  exact (Fact.out : Irreducible F).prime

/-- A polynomial lies in the homogeneous ideal `(G)` of the curve `G = 0` iff `G` divides it. -/
theorem mem_ideal_iff {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {G H : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R}
    (hG : G.IsHomogeneous d) : H ∈ ideal hG ↔ G ∣ H := by
  rw [← HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff, toIdeal_ideal, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]

end TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectivePlaneCurve

namespace PlaneCurves.Projective

variable {k : Type*} [Field k]

/-! ### Restriction of functions from `ℙⁿ` to a projective variety -/

section Variety

variable {n : ℕ} (I : HomogeneousIdeal (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) k))
  (P : zeroLocus (I : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k)))

/-- A polynomial outside the ideal of a zero `P` of `I` has a class outside the ideal of `P` in
`R ⧸ I`. -/
theorem primeCompl_pointIdeal_le_comap :
    (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl ≤
      (quotientPointIdeal I P).toIdeal.primeCompl.comap I.quotientMkGradedRingHom :=
  fun _ hf h ↦ hf (mk_mem_quotientPointIdeal_iff.1 (by simpa [HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff] using h))

/-- The restriction `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) → 𝒪_P(V)` of functions to `V = V(I)` at a zero `P` of the
homogeneous ideal `I`: the `k`-algebra hom sending `f / g` to `f̄ / ḡ`, where `f̄` is the class of
`f` in `R ⧸ I` (`toVarietyLocalRing_mk`). -/
noncomputable def toVarietyLocalRing : localRing P.1 →ₐ[k] varietyLocalRing I P where
  __ := HomogeneousLocalization.map I.quotientMkGradedRingHom (primeCompl_pointIdeal_le_comap I P)
  commutes' := HomogeneousLocalization.map_algebraMap _ I.quotientMkGradedRingHom (fun _ ↦ by
    rw [HomogeneousIdeal.quotientMkGradedRingHom_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mk_algebraMap])
    (primeCompl_pointIdeal_le_comap I P)

theorem toRingHom_toVarietyLocalRing : (toVarietyLocalRing I P : localRing P.1 →+* _) =
    HomogeneousLocalization.map I.quotientMkGradedRingHom (primeCompl_pointIdeal_le_comap I P) :=
  (rfl)

variable {I P}

/-- The restriction sends a fraction `f / g` of forms of the same degree with `g(P) ≠ 0` to the
fraction `f̄ / ḡ` of their classes. -/
theorem toVarietyLocalRing_mk
    (c : NumDenSameDeg (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) k) (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl) :
    toVarietyLocalRing I P (HomogeneousLocalization.mk c) =
      varietyLocalRing.mk ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.num.2)
        ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)
        (by simpa using localRing.eval_rep_ne_zero c.den.2 c.den_mem) := by
  change HomogeneousLocalization.map I.quotientMkGradedRingHom (primeCompl_pointIdeal_le_comap I P)
    (HomogeneousLocalization.mk c) = _
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.map_mk, varietyLocalRing.mk_def]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp

variable (I P)

/-- The restriction `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) → 𝒪_P(V)` is surjective. -/
theorem toVarietyLocalRing_surjective : Function.Surjective (toVarietyLocalRing I P) := by
  intro z
  obtain ⟨d, f, g, hf, hg, hgP, rfl⟩ := varietyLocalRing.exists_eq_mk z
  refine ⟨mk ⟨d, ⟨f, (mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 hf⟩,
    ⟨g, (mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 hg⟩,
    (mem_pointIdeal_iff_of_isHomogeneous hg).not.2 hgP⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [toVarietyLocalRing_mk]

variable [I.toIdeal.IsPrime]

/-- **The kernel of the restriction.** For a homogeneous prime `I` and `P ∈ V(I)`, the kernel of
the restriction `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) → 𝒪_P(V)` is the localized ideal `I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)`: a fraction `f / g`
vanishes on `V` iff it is `a / s` with `a ∈ I`. -/
theorem ker_toVarietyLocalRing :
    RingHom.ker (toVarietyLocalRing I P) = localIdeal P.1 I.toIdeal := by
  have key (c : NumDenSameDeg (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) k)
      (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl) :
      toVarietyLocalRing I P (HomogeneousLocalization.mk c) = 0 ↔
        (c.num : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k) ∈ I := by
    rw [toVarietyLocalRing_mk, varietyLocalRing.mk_def, ext_iff_val, val_mk, val_zero,
      Localization.mk_eq_mk', IsLocalization.mk'_eq_zero_iff]
    refine ⟨fun ⟨⟨m, hm⟩, h⟩ ↦ HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff.1 (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1
      ((mul_eq_zero.1 h).resolve_left fun hm0 ↦
        hm (by rw [show m = 0 from hm0]; exact zero_mem _))),
      fun h ↦ ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
    simp [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff.2 h)]
  refine le_antisymm (fun z hz ↦ ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective z
    exact mk_mem_localIdeal c ((key c).1 hz)
  · intro z hz
    obtain ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩ := mem_localIdeal_iff.1 hz
    exact (key c).2 hc

/-- **`𝒪_P(V) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ⧸ I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)`.** For a homogeneous prime `I` and `P ∈ V(I)`, the
restriction of functions induces an isomorphism of the quotient of `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)` by the localized
ideal `I 𝒪_P(ℙⁿ)` with `𝒪_P(V)`, sending the class of `f / g` to `f̄ / ḡ`. -/
noncomputable def quotientLocalIdealEquiv :
    (localRing P.1 ⧸ localIdeal P.1 I.toIdeal) ≃ₐ[k] varietyLocalRing I P :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k (ker_toVarietyLocalRing I P).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (toVarietyLocalRing_surjective I P))

variable {I P} in
@[simp]
theorem quotientLocalIdealEquiv_mk (z : localRing P.1) :
    quotientLocalIdealEquiv I P (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) = toVarietyLocalRing I P z :=
  (rfl)

end Variety

/-! ### The function field and the local rings of a plane curve -/

section Curve

variable {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} {d : ℕ} (hF : F.IsHomogeneous d) [Fact (Irreducible F)]

/-- The function field `k(C)` of the irreducible projective plane curve `C : F = 0`: the field of
fractions `f / g` of forms of the same degree with `F ∤ g`, the function field of the homogeneous
prime `(F)`. -/
abbrev functionField : Type _ :=
  ProjectiveSpace.functionField (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF)

theorem functionField_def :
    functionField hF = ProjectiveSpace.functionField (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) :=
  (rfl)

noncomputable example : Field (functionField hF) := inferInstance

omit [Fact (Irreducible F)] in
/-- A point of `ℙ²` lies on `C : F = 0` iff `F` vanishes at it. -/
theorem mem_zeroLocus_ideal_iff {P : ℙ k (Fin 3 → k)} :
    P ∈ zeroLocus (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)) ↔
      eval P.rep F = 0 := by
  have h : (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)) = Ideal.span {F} := by
    ext
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, SetLike.mem_coe, ← HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff,
      projectivePlaneCurve.toIdeal_ideal]
  rw [h, ProjectiveSpace.zeroLocus_span,
    ProjectiveSpace.mem_zeroLocus_iff_eval_rep (by simpa using ⟨d, hF⟩)]
  simp

variable (P : zeroLocus (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)))

/-- The local ring `𝒪_P(C)` of the irreducible projective plane curve `C : F = 0` at a point
`P ∈ C`, as a local subring of `k(C)`: the rational functions `f / g` with `f`, `g` forms of the
same degree and `g(P) ≠ 0` (`mem_localSubring_iff`). -/
noncomputable abbrev localSubring : LocalSubring (functionField hF) :=
  ProjectiveSpace.localSubring (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P

theorem localSubring_def :
    localSubring hF P = ProjectiveSpace.localSubring (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P :=
  (rfl)

variable {hF P} in
/-- An element of `k(C)` lies in `𝒪_P(C)` iff it is a fraction `f / g` of forms of the same
degree with `g(P) ≠ 0`. -/
theorem mem_localSubring_iff {z : functionField hF} :
    z ∈ (localSubring hF P).toSubring ↔
      ∃ (d : ℕ) (f g : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) (hf : f.IsHomogeneous d)
        (hg : g.IsHomogeneous d) (hgP : eval P.1.rep g ≠ 0),
        z = functionField.mk hf hg (notMem_of_eval_rep_ne_zero P.2 hg hgP) :=
  ProjectiveSpace.mem_localSubring_iff

/-- The restriction `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` of functions to `C`, sending `G / H` to `Ḡ / H̄`
(`coe_toLocalSubring_mk`). It is surjective (`toLocalSubring_surjective`) with kernel `(F_*)`
(`ker_toLocalSubring`). -/
noncomputable def toLocalSubring : localRing P.1 →ₐ[k] (localSubring hF P).toSubring :=
  (localSubringEquiv (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P).toAlgHom.comp
    (toVarietyLocalRing (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P)

theorem toLocalSubring_def : toLocalSubring hF P =
    (localSubringEquiv (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P).toAlgHom.comp
      (toVarietyLocalRing (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P) :=
  (rfl)

variable {hF P} in
/-- The restriction to `C` sends a fraction `G / H` of forms of the same degree with
`H(P) ≠ 0` to the rational function `G / H` on `C`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_toLocalSubring_mk
    (c : NumDenSameDeg (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) k) (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl) :
    (toLocalSubring hF P (HomogeneousLocalization.mk c) : functionField hF) =
      functionField.mk ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.num.2)
        ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)
        (notMem_of_eval_rep_ne_zero P.2 ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)
          (by simpa using localRing.eval_rep_ne_zero c.den.2 c.den_mem)) := by
  rw [toLocalSubring_def, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.toAlgHom_apply, coe_localSubringEquiv,
    toVarietyLocalRing_mk, varietyLocalRing.toFunctionField_mk]

/-- The restriction `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` is surjective. -/
theorem toLocalSubring_surjective : Function.Surjective (toLocalSubring hF P) :=
  (localSubringEquiv _ P).surjective.comp (toVarietyLocalRing_surjective _ P)

/-- **The kernel of `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` is `(F_*)`.** It does not depend on the choice of the
local equation `F_*`, since any two choices are associated (`associated_localEquation_mk`). -/
theorem ker_toLocalSubring :
    RingHom.ker (toLocalSubring hF P) = Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F} := by
  have h : RingHom.ker (toLocalSubring hF P) =
      RingHom.ker (toVarietyLocalRing (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) P) := by
    ext z
    simp [RingHom.mem_ker, toLocalSubring_def]
  rw [h, ker_toVarietyLocalRing, projectivePlaneCurve.toIdeal_ideal, localIdeal_span_singleton hF]

/-- `F_*` vanishes on `C`. -/
@[simp]
theorem toLocalSubring_localEquation : toLocalSubring hF P (localEquation P.1 F) = 0 := by
  rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, ker_toLocalSubring]
  exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _

/-- **`𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*)`.** The restriction of functions to `C` induces an isomorphism
of `𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*)` with the local ring `𝒪_P(C)` of the curve, sending the class of `G / H` to
`Ḡ / H̄`. -/
noncomputable def quotientLocalEquationEquiv :
    (localRing P.1 ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F}) ≃ₐ[k] (localSubring hF P).toSubring :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k (ker_toLocalSubring hF P).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (toLocalSubring_surjective hF P))

variable {hF P} in
@[simp]
theorem quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk (z : localRing P.1) :
    quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) = toLocalSubring hF P z :=
  (rfl)

variable {hF P} in
/-- The class of a fraction `G / H` goes to the rational function `G / H` on `C`. -/
theorem coe_quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk
    (c : NumDenSameDeg (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) k) (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl) :
    (quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (HomogeneousLocalization.mk c)) :
      functionField hF) =
      functionField.mk ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.num.2)
        ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)
        (notMem_of_eval_rep_ne_zero P.2 ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)
          (by simpa using localRing.eval_rep_ne_zero c.den.2 c.den_mem)) := by
  rw [quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk, coe_toLocalSubring_mk]

/-- **The image of `(F_*, G_*)` in `𝒪_P(C)`.** For every polynomial `G`, the ideal of `𝒪_P(C)`
generated by the image of `(F_*, G_*)` is generated by the image of `G_*`. -/
theorem map_toLocalSubring_span_pair (G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) :
    (Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F, localEquation P.1 G}).map (toLocalSubring hF P) =
      Ideal.span {toLocalSubring hF P (localEquation P.1 G)} := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_pair, toLocalSubring_localEquation, Ideal.span_insert_zero]

/-- **`𝒪_P(C) ⧸ (Ḡ_*) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*, G_*)`.** For every polynomial `G`, the quotient of
`𝒪_P(C)` by the image of `G_*` is the quotient of `𝒪_P(ℙ²)` by `(F_*, G_*)`. -/
noncomputable def quotientSpanPairEquiv (G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) :
    ((localSubring hF P).toSubring ⧸ Ideal.span {toLocalSubring hF P (localEquation P.1 G)})
      ≃ₐ[k] (localRing P.1 ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F, localEquation P.1 G}) :=
  ((Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ _ (quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P).symm (by
      rw [Ideal.map_span, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, Set.image_singleton]
      congr 2
      exact ((quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P).symm_apply_apply _).symm)).trans
      (DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSupₐ k _ _)).trans
    (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k (Ideal.span_insert _ _).symm)

variable {hF P} in
/-- `quotientSpanPairEquiv` sends the class of the restriction of `z` to the class of `z`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanPairEquiv_mk (G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) (z : localRing P.1) :
    quotientSpanPairEquiv hF P G (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (toLocalSubring hF P z)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z := by
  rw [← quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk z]
  simp [quotientSpanPairEquiv, -quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk]
  rfl

end Curve


/-! ### Local equations in a chart -/

section LocalEquation

open TauCeti

variable {n : ℕ} {F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k} {d : ℕ} (hF : F.IsHomogeneous d)
  {P : ℙ k (Fin (n + 1) → k)} {i : Fin (n + 1)} (hP : P ∈ affineOpen i)

include hF in
/-- **`𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸ⁿ) ⧸ (F_(i))`.** For every form `F`, irreducible or not, and
every chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0` containing `P`, the chart isomorphism `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸ⁿ)` induces an
isomorphism of the quotients by the local equation `F_*` and by the dehomogenization `F_(i)`
(`quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_mk`). -/
noncomputable def quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv :
    (localRing P ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P F}) ≃ₐ[k]
      AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P) ⧸
        Ideal.span {algebraMap _ (AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P)) (dehomogenize i F)} :=
  Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ _ (localRing.chartEquiv i hP) (by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
    exact Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.2 (associated_chartEquiv_localEquation hF hP).symm)

theorem quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_def : quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv hF hP =
    Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ _ (localRing.chartEquiv i hP) (by
      rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
      exact Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.2
        (associated_chartEquiv_localEquation hF hP).symm) :=
  (rfl)

/-- `𝒪_P(ℙⁿ) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸ⁿ) ⧸ (F_(i))` sends the class of `z` to the class of its image
under the chart isomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_mk (z : localRing P) :
    quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv hF hP (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (localRing.chartEquiv i hP z) := by
  rw [quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_def, Ideal.quotientEquivAlg_mk]

end LocalEquation

/-! ### The function field and the local rings of a plane curve in a chart -/

section Chart

open TauCeti

variable {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} {d : ℕ} (hF : F.IsHomogeneous d) [Fact (Irreducible F)]
  {i : Fin 3}

include hF in
/-- For an irreducible form `F` with `F ∤ Xᵢ`, the ideal `(F_(i))` of the dehomogenization is
prime. -/
theorem isPrime_span_dehomogenize (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) : (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}).IsPrime :=
  projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i ▸
    isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)

variable (i) in
/-- **The function field in a chart.** For an irreducible form `F` and a coordinate `Xᵢ` with
`F ∤ Xᵢ`, the function field `k(C)` of `C : F = 0` is the function field
`k(F_(i)) = Frac (k[Y₀, Y₁] ⧸ (F_(i)))` of the dehomogenization `F_(i)` of `F` at `Xᵢ`: the
isomorphism sends `f / g` to `f_(i) / g_(i)` (`functionField.chartEquiv_mk`). -/
noncomputable def functionField.chartEquiv (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
    functionField hF ≃ₐ[k] AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}) :=
  haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
  haveI := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)
  (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.chartEquiv i
      ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)).trans
    (AffineSpace.functionField.equivOfEq (projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i))

theorem functionField.chartEquiv_def (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
    haveI := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)
    Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi =
      (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.chartEquiv i
          ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)).trans
        (AffineSpace.functionField.equivOfEq (projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The chart isomorphism `k(C) ≅ k(F_(i))` sends `f / g` to `f_(i) / g_(i)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem functionField.chartEquiv_mk (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) {m : ℕ} {f g : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k}
    (hf : f.IsHomogeneous m) (hg : g.IsHomogeneous m)
    (hgI : g ∉ projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
    Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk hf hg hgI) =
      algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}) (dehomogenize i f)) /
        algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}) (dehomogenize i g)) := by
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
  have := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)
  rw [functionField.chartEquiv_def, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    ProjectiveSpace.functionField.chartEquiv_mk,
    AffineSpace.functionField.equivOfEq_div]

/-! ### Tau Ceti's function field of the curve -/

/-- The power `Xᵢᵐ` of a coordinate with `F ∤ Xᵢ` is not in the ideal `(F)`. -/
theorem X_pow_notMem_ideal (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) (m : ℕ) : X i ^ m ∉ projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF :=
  (projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 fun h ↦
    hi ((Fact.out : Irreducible F).prime.dvd_of_dvd_pow h)

omit [Fact (Irreducible F)] in
/-- The class of a form of degree `m` lies in the degree `m • 1` part of the homogeneous coordinate
ring, the degree in which Tau Ceti's charts take numerators. -/
theorem mk_mem_quotientGrading_smul_one {m : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k}
    (hp : p.IsHomogeneous m) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).toIdeal p ∈
      (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).quotientGrading (m • 1) := by
  rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  exact (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_mem_quotientGrading hp

/-- The chart isomorphisms `k(C) ≅ k(F_(j))` followed by Tau Ceti's
`projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv` in the same chart send `p / Xᵢᵐ`, for any chart `Xᵢ`, to
the germ of the function `p / Xᵢᵐ` on `D₊(Xᵢ)`. -/
private theorem chartEquiv_trans_symm_mk {j : Fin 3} (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) (hj : ¬ F ∣ X j) {m : ℕ}
    {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} (hp : p.IsHomogeneous m) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hj
    haveI := projectivePlaneCurve.nonempty_basicOpen (hG := hF) hi
    ((Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF j hj).trans
        (projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv hF j hj).symm)
        (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk hp (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m)
          (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hi m)) =
      (projectivePlaneCurve hF).germToFunctionField _ (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection _ _
        (Away.mk _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_X_mem_quotientGrading i) m _
          (mk_mem_quotientGrading_smul_one hF hp))) := by
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hj
  have := projectivePlaneCurve.nonempty_basicOpen (hG := hF) hi
  have := projectivePlaneCurve.nonempty_basicOpen (hG := hF) hj
  -- in the chart `Xⱼ` itself, this is Tau Ceti's `functionFieldEquiv_germToFunctionField_mk`
  have key : ∀ {q : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} (hq : q.IsHomogeneous m),
      ((Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF j hj).trans
        (projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv hF j hj).symm)
        (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk hq (isHomogeneous_X_pow j m)
          (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hj m)) =
      (projectivePlaneCurve hF).germToFunctionField _ (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection _ _
        (Away.mk _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_X_mem_quotientGrading j) m _
          (mk_mem_quotientGrading_smul_one hF hq))) := fun hq ↦ by
    rw [AlgEquiv.trans_apply, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq,
      projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv_germToFunctionField_mk, functionField.chartEquiv_mk]
    simp
  -- otherwise, `p / Xᵢᵐ = (p / Xⱼᵐ) / (Xᵢᵐ / Xⱼᵐ)`, and the germs on the two charts agree
  rw [← ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk_div_mk hp (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m)
    (isHomogeneous_X_pow j m) (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hi m) (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hj m),
    map_div₀, key hp, key (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m), div_eq_iff]
  · refine Eq.symm ?_
    convert AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.germToFunctionField_awayToSection_mul _
      ((projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_X_mem_quotientGrading i)
      ((projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_X_mem_quotientGrading j) m
      (mk_mem_quotientGrading_smul_one hF hp) using 4
    simp
  · rw [← key (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m)]
    exact (AlgEquiv.injective _).ne_iff.2 (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk_ne_zero _ _ _
      (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hi m)) |>.trans_eq (map_zero _)

/-- **The function field as Tau Ceti's function field of the curve.** The function field `k(C)`
of `C : F = 0`, for an irreducible form `F`, is the function field of the integral scheme
`projectivePlaneCurve hF`, the `Proj` of `k[X₀, X₁, X₂] ⧸ (F)`: the isomorphism sends `p / Xᵢᵐ`, for
any coordinate `Xᵢ` with `F ∤ Xᵢ`, to the germ of the function `p / Xᵢᵐ` on the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)`
(`schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_mk`). -/
noncomputable def functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv :
    functionField hF ≃ₐ[k] (projectivePlaneCurve hF).functionField :=
  haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF
    (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec
  (Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF _
      (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec).trans
    (projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv hF _
      (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec).symm

theorem functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_def :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF
      (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec
    functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv hF =
      (Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF _
          (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec).trans
        (projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv hF _
          (projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)).choose_spec).symm :=
  (rfl)

/-- For every coordinate `Xᵢ` with `F ∤ Xᵢ`, the isomorphism of `k(C)` with Tau Ceti's function
field sends `p / Xᵢᵐ` to the germ of the function `p / Xᵢᵐ` on the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_mk (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i) {m : ℕ}
    {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} (hp : p.IsHomogeneous m) :
    haveI := projectivePlaneCurve.nonempty_basicOpen (hG := hF) hi
    functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv hF
        (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk hp (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m)
          (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hi m)) =
      (projectivePlaneCurve hF).germToFunctionField _ (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection _ _
        (Away.mk _ ((projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF).mk_X_mem_quotientGrading i) m _
          (mk_mem_quotientGrading_smul_one hF hp))) :=
  chartEquiv_trans_symm_mk hF hi _ hp

/-- The isomorphism of `k(C)` with Tau Ceti's function field does not depend on the chart: in
every chart `Xᵢ` with `F ∤ Xᵢ`, it is the chart isomorphism `k(C) ≅ k(F_(i))` followed by the
inverse of Tau Ceti's `projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv`. -/
theorem functionField.functionFieldEquiv_schemeFunctionFieldEquiv (hi : ¬ F ∣ X i)
    (z : functionField hF) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
    projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv hF i hi (functionField.schemeFunctionFieldEquiv hF z) =
      Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi z := by
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
  rw [← AlgEquiv.eq_symm_apply, ← AlgEquiv.trans_apply]
  obtain ⟨m, f, g, hf, hg, hgI, rfl⟩ := ProjectiveSpace.functionField.exists_eq_mk z
  rw [← ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk_div_mk hf hg (isHomogeneous_X_pow i m) hgI
    (X_pow_notMem_ideal hF hi m), map_div₀, map_div₀, schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_mk hF hi,
    schemeFunctionFieldEquiv_mk hF hi, chartEquiv_trans_symm_mk hF hi hi,
    chartEquiv_trans_symm_mk hF hi hi]

/-- **The function field of an irreducible projective plane curve is an algebraic function field
of one variable**: `k(C)` is finitely generated over `k`, of transcendence degree one. -/
theorem functionField.isFunctionField : IsFunctionField k (functionField hF) := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := projectivePlaneCurve.exists_not_dvd_X (Fact.out : Irreducible F)
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF hi
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType k (AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})) :=
    haveI := Algebra.EssFiniteType.of_isLocalization
      (R := MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})
      (AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})) (nonZeroDivisors _)
    Algebra.EssFiniteType.comp k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}) _
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType k (functionField hF) :=
    Algebra.EssFiniteType.of_surjective (Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi).symm.toAlgHom
      (Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i hi).symm.surjective
  rw [isFunctionField_iff_trdeg_eq_one]
  exact (ProjectiveSpace.trdeg_functionField_eq_iff (m := 1)
    ((projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.2 hi)).2
      ⟨F, d, Fact.out, hF, projectivePlaneCurve.toIdeal_ideal hF⟩

variable (P : zeroLocus (projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)))
  (hP : P.1 ∈ affineOpen i)
include hP

/-- For a point `P` of the irreducible curve `C : F = 0` in the chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0`, `Xᵢ ∤ F`:
otherwise `F` would be a multiple of `Xᵢ` by a constant, and `C` the line `Xᵢ = 0`. -/
theorem not_X_dvd_of_mem_affineOpen : ¬ X i ∣ F := by
  rintro ⟨G, hG⟩
  have hu := ((Fact.out : Irreducible F).isUnit_or_isUnit hG).resolve_left
    (MvPolynomial.prime_X (R := k) (σ := Fin 3) (i := i)).not_isUnit
  have h : eval P.1.rep (X i * G) = 0 := hG ▸ (mem_zeroLocus_ideal_iff hF).1 P.2
  rw [map_mul, eval_X] at h
  exact mul_ne_zero ((mem_affineOpen_iff i P.1).1 hP) (hu.map (eval P.1.rep)).ne_zero h

omit [Fact (Irreducible F)] in
/-- For a point `P` of the curve `C : F = 0` in the chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0`, `F ∤ Xᵢ`. -/
theorem not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen : ¬ F ∣ X i :=
  (projectivePlaneCurve.mem_ideal_iff hF).not.1 (X_notMem_of_mem_affineOpen P hP)

omit [Fact (Irreducible F)] in
/-- The dehomogenization `F_(i)` vanishes at the affine coordinates `φᵢ(P)` of a point `P ∈ C` in
the chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0`. -/
theorem span_dehomogenize_le_vanishingIdeal :
    Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F} ≤ MvPolynomial.vanishingIdeal k {affineChart i P.1} :=
  projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i ▸ map_dehomogenize_le_vanishingIdeal P hP

variable (i) in
/-- **The local ring in a chart.** For a point `P` of the irreducible curve `C : F = 0` in the
chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0`, the local ring `𝒪_P(C)` is the local ring `𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))` of the affine curve
`F_(i) = 0` at the affine coordinates of `P`: the restriction of `functionField.chartEquiv`
(`localSubring.coe_chartEquiv`), sending `f / g` to `f_(i) / g_(i)`. -/
noncomputable def localSubring.chartEquiv :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
    (localSubring hF P).toSubring ≃ₐ[k] (AffineSpace.localSubring (affineChart i P.1)
      (span_dehomogenize_le_vanishingIdeal hF P hP)).toSubring :=
  haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
  haveI := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ (X_notMem_of_mem_affineOpen P hP)
  ((localSubringEquiv _ P).symm.trans (varietyLocalRing.chartEquiv i P hP)).trans
    (AffineSpace.localSubring.equivOfEq _ (projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i) rfl _)

theorem localSubring.chartEquiv_def :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
    haveI := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ (X_notMem_of_mem_affineOpen P hP)
    Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP =
      ((localSubringEquiv _ P).symm.trans (varietyLocalRing.chartEquiv i P hP)).trans
        (AffineSpace.localSubring.equivOfEq _ (projectivePlaneCurve.map_dehomogenize_ideal hF i)
          rfl (span_dehomogenize_le_vanishingIdeal hF P hP)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The isomorphism `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))` is the restriction of `k(C) ≅ k(F_(i))`. -/
@[simp]
theorem localSubring.coe_chartEquiv (z : (localSubring hF P).toSubring) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
    (Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP z :
        AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})) =
      Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP) z := by
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
  have := isPrime_map_dehomogenize _ (X_notMem_of_mem_affineOpen P hP)
  rw [localSubring.chartEquiv_def, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    AffineSpace.localSubring.coe_equivOfEq, varietyLocalRing.coe_chartEquiv,
    ← coe_localSubringEquiv, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply, functionField.chartEquiv_def,
    AlgEquiv.trans_apply]

/-- The isomorphism `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))` sends the restriction to `C` of a fraction
`f / g`, `g(P) ≠ 0`, to `f_(i) / g_(i)`. -/
theorem localSubring.coe_chartEquiv_toLocalSubring_mk
    (c : NumDenSameDeg (homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) k) (pointIdeal P.1).toIdeal.primeCompl) :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
    (Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP (toLocalSubring hF P (mk c)) :
        AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})) =
      algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})
        (dehomogenize i (c.num : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k))) /
        algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})
          (dehomogenize i (c.den : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k))) := by
  rw [localSubring.coe_chartEquiv, coe_toLocalSubring_mk, functionField.chartEquiv_mk]

variable (i) in
/-- **`𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))`.** For a point `P` of the irreducible curve `C : F = 0`
in the chart `Xᵢ ≠ 0`, the local ring `𝒪_P(C)` is the quotient of `𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²)` by the
dehomogenization `F_(i)`: `localSubring.chartEquiv` followed by Problem 2.44
(`AffineSpace.quotientAlgEquiv`). It is compatible with the restriction `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)` and
the chart isomorphism `𝒪_P(ℙ²) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²)` (`localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_toLocalSubring`).
-/
noncomputable def localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv :
    (localSubring hF P).toSubring ≃ₐ[k] AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P.1) ⧸
      Ideal.span {algebraMap _ (AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P.1)) (dehomogenize i F)} :=
  haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
  (Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP).trans ((AffineSpace.quotientAlgEquiv _ _).trans
    (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k (by rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton])))

theorem localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_def :
    haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
    Projective.localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv hF i P hP =
      (Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP).trans
        ((AffineSpace.quotientAlgEquiv _ _).trans
          (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k (by rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]))) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **Compatibility with the restriction and the chart of `ℙ²`.** The restriction of `z ∈ 𝒪_P(ℙ²)`
to `C` goes to the class of the image of `z` under the chart isomorphism
`𝒪_P(ℙ²) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_toLocalSubring (z : localRing P.1) :
    Projective.localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv hF i P hP (toLocalSubring hF P z) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (localRing.chartEquiv i hP z) := by
  have := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective z
  have hb : eval (affineChart i P.1) (dehomogenize i (c.den : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)) ≠ 0 :=
    (eval_affineChart_dehomogenize_eq_zero_iff hP ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 c.den.2)).not.2
      (by simpa using localRing.eval_rep_ne_zero c.den.2 c.den_mem)
  rw [localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_def, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    AffineSpace.quotientAlgEquiv_eq_mk_mk' _ _ hb
      (localSubring.coe_chartEquiv_toLocalSubring_mk hF P hP c),
    Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk, localRing.chartEquiv_mk]

/-- The isomorphisms `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*)`, `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))` and
`𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))` commute. -/
theorem localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_quotientLocalEquationEquiv
    (z : localRing P.1 ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F}) :
    Projective.localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv hF i P hP (quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P z) =
      quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv hF hP z := by
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective z
  rw [quotientLocalEquationEquiv_mk, localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_toLocalSubring,
    quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_mk]

omit hP

/-- **The local ring of an irreducible projective plane curve as a quotient and in affine
charts.** Let `F` be an irreducible form of degree `d`, `C : F = 0` and `P ∈ C`.

* (a) The restriction `𝒪_P(ℙ²) → 𝒪_P(C)`, `G / H ↦ Ḡ / H̄`, is surjective with kernel `(F_*)`,
  so that `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*)`, and `𝒪_P(C) ⧸ (Ḡ_*) ≅ 𝒪_P(ℙ²) ⧸ (F_*, G_*)` for every
  polynomial `G`.
* (b) For every coordinate `Xᵢ` with `Xᵢ(P) ≠ 0`, the dehomogenization `F_(i)` is irreducible of
  total degree `d`; there is an isomorphism `k(C) ≅ k(F_(i))` sending `f / g` to
  `f_(i) / g_(i)`; it restricts to an isomorphism `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(F_(i))`; and there is an
  isomorphism `𝒪_P(C) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (F_(i))` compatible with the restriction of (a) and the
  chart isomorphism `𝒪_P(ℙ²) ≅ 𝒪_{φᵢ(P)}(𝔸²)`.
* For every form `G`, irreducible or not, and every point `Q` with `Xⱼ(Q) ≠ 0`, the chart
  isomorphism induces `𝒪_Q(ℙ²) ⧸ (G_*) ≅ 𝒪_{φⱼ(Q)}(𝔸²) ⧸ (G_(j))`.

The isomorphisms are `quotientLocalEquationEquiv`, `quotientSpanPairEquiv`,
`functionField.chartEquiv`, `localSubring.chartEquiv`, `localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv` and
`quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv`.

Milestone: *Local ring of an irreducible projective plane curve as a quotient and in affine
charts*. -/
theorem localSubring_spec :
    -- (a)
    (Function.Surjective (toLocalSubring hF P) ∧
      RingHom.ker (toLocalSubring hF P) = Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F} ∧
      Nonempty ((localRing P.1 ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F}) ≃ₐ[k]
        (localSubring hF P).toSubring) ∧
      ∀ G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k,
        Nonempty (((localSubring hF P).toSubring ⧸
            Ideal.span {toLocalSubring hF P (localEquation P.1 G)}) ≃ₐ[k]
          (localRing P.1 ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation P.1 F, localEquation P.1 G}))) ∧
    -- (b)
    (∀ (i : Fin 3) (hP : P.1 ∈ affineOpen i),
      haveI := isPrime_span_dehomogenize hF (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)
      Irreducible (dehomogenize i F) ∧ (dehomogenize i F).totalDegree = d ∧
        ∃ e : functionField hF ≃ₐ[k] AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F}),
          (∀ (m : ℕ) (f g : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) (hf : f.IsHomogeneous m)
            (hg : g.IsHomogeneous m) (hgI : g ∉ projectivePlaneCurve.ideal hF),
            e (ProjectiveSpace.functionField.mk hf hg hgI) =
              algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})
                (dehomogenize i f)) /
                algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})
                  (dehomogenize i g))) ∧
          (∃ e' : (localSubring hF P).toSubring ≃ₐ[k] (AffineSpace.localSubring
              (affineChart i P.1) (span_dehomogenize_le_vanishingIdeal hF P hP)).toSubring,
            ∀ z, (e' z : AffineSpace.functionField (Ideal.span {dehomogenize i F})) = e z) ∧
          ∃ e'' : (localSubring hF P).toSubring ≃ₐ[k]
              AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P.1) ⧸ Ideal.span
                {algebraMap _ (AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart i P.1)) (dehomogenize i F)},
            ∀ z : localRing P.1,
              e'' (toLocalSubring hF P z) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (localRing.chartEquiv i hP z)) ∧
    -- the general form
    ∀ (G : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k) (e : ℕ), G.IsHomogeneous e →
      ∀ (Q : ℙ k (Fin 3 → k)) (j : Fin 3) (hQ : Q ∈ affineOpen j),
        ∃ φ : (localRing Q ⧸ Ideal.span {localEquation Q G}) ≃ₐ[k]
            AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart j Q) ⧸ Ideal.span
              {algebraMap _ (AffineSpace.localRing k (affineChart j Q)) (dehomogenize j G)},
          ∀ z, φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (localRing.chartEquiv j hQ z) :=
  ⟨⟨toLocalSubring_surjective hF P, ker_toLocalSubring hF P,
      ⟨quotientLocalEquationEquiv hF P⟩, fun G ↦ ⟨quotientSpanPairEquiv hF P G⟩⟩,
    fun i hP ↦ ⟨(irreducible_dehomogenize_iff hF (not_X_dvd_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP)).2
        Fact.out, totalDegree_dehomogenize_of_not_X_dvd hF (not_X_dvd_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP),
      Projective.functionField.chartEquiv hF i (not_dvd_X_of_mem_affineOpen hF P hP),
      fun _ _ _ hf hg hgI ↦ functionField.chartEquiv_mk hF _ hf hg hgI,
      ⟨Projective.localSubring.chartEquiv hF i P hP, localSubring.coe_chartEquiv hF P hP⟩,
      Projective.localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv hF i P hP,
      localSubring.chartQuotientEquiv_toLocalSubring hF P hP⟩,
    fun _ _ hG _ _ hQ ↦ ⟨quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv hG hQ,
      quotientLocalEquationChartEquiv_mk hG hQ⟩⟩

end Chart

end PlaneCurves.Projective

